{
  "name": "Exercise sEt 4.1",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "9-math-3-ex4.1-q1",
      "questionNumber": 1,
      "question": "Using the identity $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$, expand the following: **(i)** $(7x + 4y)^2$ **(ii)** $\\left(\\frac{7}{5}x + \\frac{3}{2}y\\right)^2$ **(iii)** $(2.5p + 1.5q)^2$ **(iv)** $\\left(\\frac{3}{4}s + 8t\\right)^2$ **(v)** $\\left(x + \\frac{1}{2y}\\right)^2$ **(vi)** $\\left(\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y}\\right)^2$",
      "solution": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "content": "**Recall the identity:** $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$."
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "content": "**(i) $(7x + 4y)^2$:** Here $a = 7x$ and $b = 4y$. $$(7x)^2 + 2(7x)(4y) + (4y)^2 = 49x^2 + 56xy + 16y^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "content": "**(ii) $\\left(\\frac{7}{5}x + \\frac{3}{2}y\\right)^2$:** Here $a = \\frac{7}{5}x$ and $b = \\frac{3}{2}y$. $$\\left(\\frac{7}{5}x\\right)^2 + 2\\left(\\frac{7}{5}x\\right)\\left(\\frac{3}{2}y\\right) + \\left(\\frac{3}{2}y\\right)^2 = \\frac{49}{25}x^2 + \\frac{21}{5}xy + \\frac{9}{4}y^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 4,
          "content": "**(iii) $(2.5p + 1.5q)^2$:** Here $a = 2.5p$ and $b = 1.5q$. $$(2.5p)^2 + 2(2.5p)(1.5q) + (1.5q)^2 = 6.25p^2 + 7.5pq + 2.25q^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 5,
          "content": "**(iv) $\\left(\\frac{3}{4}s + 8t\\right)^2$:** Here $a = \\frac{3}{4}s$ and $b = 8t$. $$\\left(\\frac{3}{4}s\\right)^2 + 2\\left(\\frac{3}{4}s\\right)(8t) + (8t)^2 = \\frac{9}{16}s^2 + 12st + 64t^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 6,
          "content": "**(v) $\\left(x + \\frac{1}{2y}\\right)^2$:** Here $a = x$ and $b = \\frac{1}{2y}$. $$x^2 + 2(x)\\left(\\frac{1}{2y}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{1}{2y}\\right)^2 = x^2 + \\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{1}{4y^2}$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 7,
          "content": "**(vi) $\\left(\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y}\\right)^2$:** Here $a = \\frac{1}{x}$ and $b = \\frac{1}{y}$. $$\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 + 2\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{y}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{1}{y}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{x^2} + \\frac{2}{xy} + \\frac{1}{y^2}$$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "(i) 49x² + 56xy + 16y²  (ii) (49/25)x² + (21/5)xy + (9/4)y²  (iii) 6.25p² + 7.5pq + 2.25q²  (iv) (9/16)s² + 12st + 64t²  (v) x² + x/y + 1/(4y²)  (vi) 1/x² + 2/(xy) + 1/y²",
      "verified": true,
      "formulaBox": {
        "title": "Square of a Sum",
        "content": "$$(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$$"
      },
      "notes": "**Exam Tip:** Square each term separately, then add twice the product of the two terms. Be careful with fractions — square numerator and denominator separately."
    },
    {
      "id": "9-math-3-ex4.1-q2",
      "questionNumber": 2,
      "question": "Using the same identity, find the values of the following: **(i)** $(64)^2$ **(ii)** $(105)^2$ **(iii)** $(205)^2$",
      "solution": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "content": "**(i) $(64)^2$:** Write $64 = 60 + 4$. $$(60 + 4)^2 = 60^2 + 2 \\times 60 \\times 4 + 4^2 = 3600 + 480 + 16 = 4096$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "content": "**(ii) $(105)^2$:** Write $105 = 100 + 5$. $$(100 + 5)^2 = 100^2 + 2 \\times 100 \\times 5 + 5^2 = 10000 + 1000 + 25 = 11025$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "content": "**(iii) $(205)^2$:** Write $205 = 200 + 5$. $$(200 + 5)^2 = 200^2 + 2 \\times 200 \\times 5 + 5^2 = 40000 + 2000 + 25 = 42025$$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "(i) 4096  (ii) 11025  (iii) 42025",
      "verified": true,
      "notes": "**Exam Tip:** Splitting a number into a round number plus a small number makes squaring much easier using the identity."
    }
  ]
}
